# What the `complexity delta` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml installs.
# This is the file a person edits. requirements.txt beside it is the lock
# file made from it: the same version plus everything it depends on, each
# with the SHA256 checksums pip must see before it installs the file.
#
# Pinned, not floating. A tokenizer change between lizard releases moves
# every number the check compares, which would read as a pull request that
# added complexity on the day the release landed.
#
# After changing the line, rebuild the lock from this folder, on the Python
# the job uses (3.15):
#
#   pip-compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
lizard==1.24.0
